{"version":"1","id":"hasura","handle":"hasura","name":"Hasura","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/9e128def97fd4e9198d016b2dc1cbd6e","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-0.2664,"y":-2.4183,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":227,"newest_post_at":"2024-04-30T17:34:57.782Z","oldest_post_at":"2021-06-10T14:44:41.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.015419,"listicle_ratio":0.022026,"question_ratio":0.004405,"avg_read_time":5.185022,"summary_length_avg":319.040541,"title_length_avg":55.268722,"title_length_var":257.597392,"tag_entropy":3.790683,"tag_diversity":0.651982,"top_tag_share":0.22467,"avg_upvotes":1.572687,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.061674,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.041899,"zero_engagement_share":0.537445,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":1.50603,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.060748},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-1.5882,2.5147],"cadence_depth":[3.5441,-1.9118],"hype_variety":[3.5441,5.9706],"title_style":[-3.1176,5.5294]},"top_tags":[["graphql",203],["database",54],["postgresql",30],["cloud",29],["general-programming",23],["performance",22],["security",22],["backend",21]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Next.js 13 Nested Layouts, Streaming SSR with Realtime GraphQL","Building real-time chat apps with GraphQL streaming subscriptions","Why we deleted 95% of our E2E tests"],"outlier":["How our marketing ops team built a realtime lead-to-account matching solution with Hasura, BigQuery, Zapier and Salesforce."]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"xCzAU8tu6","title":"Introducing TypeScript functions on Hasura DDN","url":"https://hasura.io/blog/introducing-typescript-functions-on-hasura-ddn","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/introducing-typescript-functions-on-hasura-ddn-xczau8tu6","summary":"Hasura DDN introduces TypeScript functions to simplify GraphQL server development. It allows you to integrate custom business logic, perform data transformations, and access data from unsupported sources. TypeScript functions provide type safety, error handling, and observability. They can leverage any NPM package and simplify complex tasks. Hasura DDN also supports joining data from different sources and enhances observability with OpenTelemetry.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/aa4eac11ee1c82ddb5d783b71feb0e08?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-30T17:34:57.782Z"},{"id":"1GFPQt4MJ","title":"Consolidated data access in Hasura DDN with data connectors","url":"https://hasura.io/blog/consolidated-data-access-in-hasura-ddn-with-data-connectors","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/consolidated-data-access-in-hasura-ddn-with-data-connectors-1gfpqt4mj","summary":"Hasura v3 introduces the use of data connectors to consolidate data access to data sources. The new NDC specification allows for easier development of connectors and provides benefits such as increased flexibility, scalability, and efficiency.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4317584b762b3a18ed05812b604a1bf9?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-29T18:23:22.590Z"},{"id":"zNuz0Ygrh","title":"Introducing Hasura DDN multi-region database routing","url":"https://hasura.io/blog/global-reach-local-performance-introducing-hasuras-multi-region-database-routing","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/introducing-hasura-ddn-multi-region-database-routing-znuz0ygrh","summary":"Hasura DDN is a data delivery network that offers multi-region support for delivering data from the edge. It provides instant GraphQL APIs on a variety of data sources, positioned close to users around the globe. Hasura DDN routes requests to the nearest database location configured by the user, ensuring low latency and high availability.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5ebc8816d0fe53f4fbbfcb4a603e1e08?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2024-04-29T14:16:30.836Z"},{"id":"M8qQ0jMaZ","title":"A practical guide for your GraphQL adoption journey","url":"https://hasura.io/blog/graphql-maturity-model-a-practical-guide-for-your-graphql-adoption-journey","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-practical-guide-for-your-graphql-adoption-journey-m8qq0jmaz","summary":"This post discusses the GraphQL maturity model and the stages involved in adopting GraphQL. It also covers implementation patterns and tools for building GraphQL APIs.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/57c7c99e5ff6e25d7ade4dcd4b3a6b00?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-25T13:56:36.079Z"},{"id":"qvyiR9pKs","title":"Hasura DDN: The most incredible API for ClickHouse","url":"https://hasura.io/blog/hasura-ddn-the-most-incredible-api-for-clickhouse","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/hasura-ddn-the-most-incredible-api-for-clickhouse-qvyir9pks","summary":"Hasura DDN enables developers to build and scale applications effortlessly by creating a supergraph that simplifies microservices. ClickHouse is a powerful columnar database for real-time analytics. It is ideal for scenarios with large volumes of data and read-heavy operations. ClickHouse views and projections can optimize query performance.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/101f5b3a716f640b7242c260cfe6cbdc?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-16T16:14:01.537Z"},{"id":"05SB2rxpX","title":"Announcing Hasura DDN in beta \u2013 now open for sign-ups!","url":"https://hasura.io/blog/announcing-hasura-ddn-in-beta-now-open-for-sign-ups","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/announcing-hasura-ddn-in-beta-now-open-for-sign-ups--05sb2rxpx","summary":"Hasura DDN is a next-generation API platform that delivers on-demand data composability with a focus on supergraph architecture. It offers a domain-first approach for modeling supergraphs, optimized API performance, and a superior developer experience.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f75e2e81b0c0f1a3fbd33b51056f189a?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-04T21:38:17.921Z"},{"id":"Lf8rczvG1","title":"Announcing Hasura Data Delivery Network in beta","url":"https://hasura.io/blog/announcing-hasura-data-delivery-network-in-beta","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/announcing-hasura-data-delivery-network-in-beta-lf8rczvg1","summary":"Hasura has launched their next-generation product, the Hasura Data Delivery Network (DDN), which provides a stable and secure API on dynamic data and code. It offers automatic API contracts, frictionless CI/CD, and scalable APIs without a cost impact. Hasura DDN enables composable APIs and federated development, tackling challenges of performance, composability, and maintenance in GraphQL platform teams. Hasura DDN is available for enterprise use cases.","image":"https://hasura.io/blog/content/images/2024/04/DDN-og-motion-1.gif","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-02T22:43:31.598Z"},{"id":"LBR4jdm36","title":"Designing a feature-rich, high-performance, domain-driven GraphQL API","url":"https://hasura.io/blog/compile-dont-resolve-designing-a-feature-rich-high-performance-domain-driven-graphql-api","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/designing-a-feature-rich-high-performance-domain-driven-graphql-api-lbr4jdm36","summary":"Learn about designing a feature-rich, high-performance, domain-driven GraphQL API using Hasura's approach. Compare the schema-first approach to the domain-driven approach. Explore how to optimize performance and leverage database capabilities.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/06373f366c990929e7e4cd38784a207c?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-03-28T20:32:32.682Z"},{"id":"bTP8kfyFI","title":"Building a GraphQL server with 